    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented threshold support for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**1. frai-core/src/eval/index.js**\n- Updated `generateReport()` to accept an optional `thresholds` parameter (e.g., `{ exact_match: 0.9 }`)\n- When thresholds are provided, the report includes:\n  - `passed` (boolean): true if all thresholds pass\n  - `thresholds` (array): one entry per threshold with `{ metric, min, score, passed }`\n- Metrics with null scores fail their thresholds\n\n**2. frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js**\n- Updated markdown output to include a \"## Thresholds\" section\n- Shows PASS/FAIL status for each threshold with min and actual score\n\n**3. frai-cli/src/index.ts**\n- Added `--threshold <metric=min>` option (repeatable, e.g., `--threshold exact_match=0.9`)\n- Parses and validates threshold format (metric=number, value 0-1)\n- Exit codes:\n  - **0**: Success (all thresholds pass or no thresholds specified)\n  - **1**: Threshold failure (report written regardless)\n  - **2**: Usage error (malformed threshold, unknown metric, or invalid value) \u2014 no report written, lists valid metrics\n- Reports are written in all cases except usage errors\n\n**4. frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js**\n- Added 4 comprehensive tests covering:\n  - Passing thresholds\n  - Failing thresholds  \n  - Null score behavior\n  - No-threshold backward compatibility\n\n### Verification\n\n\u2705 **Test Results**: 30 tests passing (+4 new threshold tests)  \n\u2705 **Exit Codes**: Correct behavior for all scenarios (0, 1, 2)  \n\u2705 **Formats**: Both JSON and Markdown reports work correctly  \n\u2705 **Backward Compatibility**: Without `--threshold`, behavior is unchanged  \n\u2705 **Error Handling**: Clear error messages with valid metric list for unknown metrics  \n\nThe feature is ready for use with commands like:\n```bash\nfrai eval --outputs outputs.json --references refs.json \\\n  --threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.8\n```",
